&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Germanic languages include: Afrikaans, Danish, Dutch, English, Faroese, Frisian, German, Icelandic, Limburgish, Low German, Luxembourgish, Norwegian, Scots, Swedish and Yiddish.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. Fifth stage discolouration has been determined via autopsy.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. In &lt;em&gt;Fifty Thousand Words to Defeat the Red Menace,&lt;/em&gt; a mass market paperback novel published in 1971 supposedly capable of &amp;quot;defusing the threat to international life and liberty currently festering behind the Iron Curtain&amp;quot; if read.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-4&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;4&lt;/a&gt;. In a series of patriotic posters published during the Great War.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-5&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;5&lt;/a&gt;. In an online sensitivity seminar entitled &amp;quot;How to Not Be Lou Dobbs&amp;quot; subsequently adopted, with minor modifications, by the Foundation for internal use.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-6&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;6&lt;/a&gt;. In &lt;em&gt;Polk the Lazy Cat,&lt;/em&gt; a comic strip published daily between 1962 and 1987.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-7&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;7&lt;/a&gt;. Pre-modern Germany.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-8&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;8&lt;/a&gt;. The Greek city of Candia, now Heraklion, did not boast a school of medicine until the establishment of the University of Crete in the 1970s. The Principality of Andorra, being a principality, has neither kings nor queens. No European monarchy has ever officially titled its heads of state &amp;quot;Regis&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Regina.&amp;quot; The image used to represent &amp;quot;Doctor Braun&amp;quot; is a sketch of Sir Mackenzie Bowell, Prime Minister of Canada from 1894 to 1896.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-9&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;9&lt;/a&gt;. The Germans first used chlorine gas against Canadian and French troops at the Second Battle of Ypres, 22 April 1915.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-10&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;10&lt;/a&gt;. Sir Frederick Grant Banting, Acroamatic Abatement Section researcher and co-discoverer of insulin with Charles Herbert Best.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-11&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;11&lt;/a&gt;. Victory in Europe Day, the date of Germany&#039;s surrender to the Allies at the close of the Second World War.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-12&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;12&lt;/a&gt;. Victory in the Pacific Day, the date of Japan&#039;s surrender to the Allies after the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The date is 15 August outside of North America, due to time zone differences.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-13&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;13&lt;/a&gt;. By this time several equally commercial, less overtly-caustic copycats had begun publication.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-222322-14&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;14&lt;/a&gt;. Examples include aventurine, hematite, white onyx and, on one occasion, talc.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5381&quot;&gt;SCP-5381&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-5382 | &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5383&quot;&gt;SCP-5383&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6479803&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607523819&quot; alt=&quot;HarryBlank&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6479803)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank&quot;  &gt;HarryBlank&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
